    "title": "Liber 777 vel Prolegomena Symbolica ad Systemam Sceptico-Mysticae Viae Explicandae, Fundamentum Hieroglyphicum Sanctissimorum Scientiae Summae (Aleister Crowley)",
    "year": 1909,
    "url_used": [
      "https://archive.org/download/Birdsfrogsandmirrors/AleisterCrowley-Liber777.pdf (local text extraction 777.txt = Celephaïs Press e-text of 777 Revised)",
      "https://archive.org/download/theqabalahofaleistercrowleythreetexts/The%20Qabalah%20of%20Aleister%20Crowley%20Three%20Texts_djvu.txt (archive.org OCR of the scanned Weiser facsimile 'The Qabalah of Aleister Crowley', reproducing the 777 Revised tables, themselves facsimiles of 1909)",
      "https://archive.org/download/Liber777Revised/Liber777revised_djvu.txt (OCR of a later Celephaïs revision, 2004; used only to spot-check e-text variants, not independent)"
    ],
    "method": "The local PDF text extraction emits table cells one per line in row order (key number, then each column's cell, right-hand page columns in order). Each table page was collapsed into a single delimited stream (dropping dot-leader lines and re-joining hyphen splits) and read row by row by key number. That gave the base reading. Every cell for keys 1-32 in the god, colour, stone, plant, animal, perfume, weapon and vegetable-drug columns was then compared against the archive.org OCR of an independent scanned facsimile, the Weiser printing. Where the two disagreed and the scan was legible, the scan reading was kept as the 1909 text and the variant was logged under problems. 777's own column notes resolved several cases. The e-text's [[...]] additions from 777 Revised were moved into per-key 'revised_additions'. Symbol-font glyphs were turned into element and planet words. Nothing was filled from memory.",
    "excluded": "Crowley's later additions from 777 Revised (1955) are omitted: only the 1909 tables are included."
  },
