  "problems": [
    "Columns 'archangel' and 'choir' are 777 Col. XCIX 'Archangels of Assiah' and Col. C 'Angels of Assiah'. 777 itself does NOT label these Briah/Yetzirah. Its Briah columns are LXXXV 'Angels of Briah' and LXXXVI 'Choirs of Angels in Briah' (a different list: Yehuel, Raphael, Kerubiel...), given as extra fields briah_angel/briah_choir. The 1909 facsimile prints all four columns in Hebrew only. The transliterations come from the Celephaïs e-text alone. I checked them against that e-text's own Hebrew letters, but could not check them against the scan (its Hebrew OCR is unreadable).",
    "Col. C note in 777: the choir order is from R. Mosheh ben Maimon; R. Ishmael and the book Pliah give another order (Cherubim, Chasmalim, Chaioth, Aralim, Seraphim, Tarshishim, Auphanim, Auphanim, Aishim, Taphsarim). Col. XCIX note adds Azrael and Israfel among archangels (no key given).",
    "prince_scale/princess_scale are 777's 'Emperor Scale' (Col. XVII) and 'Empress Scale' (Col. XVIII).",
    "Astrological and elemental glyphs were rendered as words. The Celephaïs symbol-font letters were decoded from internal context (B=Fire, C=Water, D=Air, E=Earth, '='=Moon): 'Cherub of Air/Earth/Fire/Water' (animals 11, 16, 19, 23, 28, 31), Egyptian 23 'Auramoth (as Water)', Greek 9 'Zeus (as Air)', Roman 9 'Diana (as Moon)', plants 13 'Hazel (as Moon)', weapons 31 'Pyramid of Fire'. Egyptian 23 and the Fire/Water/Air/Earth cherubs are confirmed by 777's own notes. Greek 9 'as Air' rests only on the glyph letter 'D', and the scan OCR shows an ambiguous triangle.",
    "Perfumes 26: 'Musk, Civet (also [planet symbol]ian Perfumes)'. The planet glyph is unreadable in both copies (likely Saturnian, but not confirmed). Left as a placeholder.",
    "Celephaïs e-text vs 1909/1955 facsimile scan disagreements; the scan reading was used. Roman 3: scan 'Juno, Cybele, Saturn, Hecate, &c.' (e-text omits Saturn). Stones 4: scan 'Amethyst and Sapphire' (e-text 'Amethyst, Sapphire'). Stones 11: scan 'Topaz, Chalcedony' (e-text 'Topaz' only, with [[Chalcedony]] moved to 28). Animals 11: scan 'Eagle or Man' (e-text 'Eagle, Man'). Animals 14: scan 'Sparrow, Dove, Swan' (e-text 'Sparrow, Dove [[Sow]]'; the 2004 e-text has '[[Swan, Sow, birds generally]]'). Animals 24: scan 'Scorpion, Beetle, Lobster or Crayfish, Wolf' (e-text 'Scorpio, Beetle, Crayfish or Lobster, Wolf'). Plants 12: scan 'Marjolane' (e-text 'Major-lane'). Plants 30: scan 'Sunflower, Laurel, Heliotrope' (e-text 'Laural, Heliotrop'). Egyptian 28: 'Ahephi' per scan and notes (e-text 'Ahepi'). Egyptian 14: scan 'Hathoor' (e-text 'Hathor').",
    "Colour-scale disagreements; the scan reading was used. Empress 8 'Yellowish brown, flecked white' (e-text 'Yellow-brown'). Empress 10 'Black rayed with yellow'. Empress 14 'Bright rose or cerise' (e-text 'of cerise'). Empress 23 adds 'like mother-of-pearl'. Empress 26 'approaching black' (e-text 'near black'). Empress 27 'rayed azure or emerald' (e-text 'azure or orange'). Emperor 28 'Bluish mauve'. Emperor 29 'pinkish' (e-text 'pinksh'). Queen 31 / Empress 31 'Vermilion' (e-text 'Vermillion').",
    "Emperor scale 15 'Brilliant flame' is from the e-text only; the scan OCR dropped that cell.",
    "Egyptian 11 'Nu' is missing from the scan OCR. It is taken from the e-text and confirmed by 777's note on Col. XIX ('Nu is the Lord of the Firmament'). Egyptian 23: the scan OCR reads 'Tum Athph Auramoth'; 'Tum, Ptah' follows the e-text and 777's note ('Ptah as the Mummy').",
    "Stones 30 is spelled 'Crysolith' in the e-text table and OCR'd 'Crysoleth' from the scan. 777's note spells it 'Chrysolith'. The e-text table spelling was kept.",
    "Animals 6: scan 'Phoenix' (e-text lost the œ ligature: 'Phnix').",
    "vegetable_drugs (Col. XLIII) is an extra field beside 'plants' (Col. XXXIX). Veg. drugs 3: scan 'Belladonna', but the e-text has 'Belladonna, Soma'. Veg. drugs 7: scan 'Damiana', but the e-text has 'Damiana, Cannabis Indica'. Veg. drugs 13: 'Juniper' per scan (e-text 'Jupiter', a typo). Veg. drugs 23: 'Cascara' per scan (e-text 'Caseara'). Keys 24, 25, 27, 31 and 32 are blank in the source and set to null.",
    "Square brackets [ ] inside values are original 777 (1909) brackets. 'revised_additions' holds the e-text's [[double-bracket]] items. Its transcriber took these from Crowley's remarks in 777 Revised (1955); they are not part of the 1909 table. Most were not checkable against the scan, which shows only the 1909 table.",
    "Single-source cells (e-text only, no independent check): all archangel/choir/briah_* transliterations and all revised_additions. Every other column was compared row by row against the scan OCR for keys 1-32. Cells not flagged above agreed, allowing for OCR noise (dot leaders, broken glyphs)."
  ]
